From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:17:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kanban sync: the pre-head push holds a status the Board has
 as done (stale wake)

Required CI on 71d46e0099 failed test_kanban_stale_wake_terminal::
test_a_wake_pushed_after_a_remote_completion_does_not_reopen_the_board_card
(#1958's acceptance): the push before the pull sent a local wake's
status=ready for a card the Board had completed in a page this host had not
pulled, so #1958's push strip (which needs the completion locally) never saw
it, and the send-time HLC reopened the card on the Board.

While a round is before the feed head (before its pulls, and after them when
the page budget left it behind) a task row whose live status is not
running/terminal, on a card the Board has acknowledged, is checked against the
Board's own row (row_evidence, one read per card per push). A done/archived
row there, or no answer, skips that card's rows until a pull reaches the head
and the strip judges them; other cards' rows still go (a wake on a live card
is still sent before page 2). Run rows keep their FIFO stop.

hold_runs -> before_head (it now holds more than run rows); the selection
moved to kanban_sync_backlog.sendable_before_head.

Test: test_a_wake_on_a_card_the_board_completed_waits_for_the_head_while_a_live_one_goes_first
(RED on 71d46e0099, GREEN here); #1958's suite is green unchanged.
